# Sub-agent policy

**Off:** prefer Task for non-trivial tool work; skip trivial single-tool answers.
**On:** system Multitask gate wins -- spawn async background subagent(s); end turn (no await/poll); one coherent worker unless workstreams are independent; self-contained prompts; model table applies.

**Spawn:** (1) set `model` from table (default `cursor-grok-4.5-low`); (2) one worker, self-contained prompt; (3) specialised skill optional.

| Role | Family | Slug |
|------|--------|------|
| Thinking / planning / architecture | Grok | `cursor-grok-4.5-low` |
| Web search / live docs fetch | Gemini | `gemini-3-flash` |
| Visual items review (UI screenshots, layout appearance, letterhead) | Kimi | `kimi-k3-max` |
| Clear-step routines | Composer | `composer-2.5` |
| MemNet snapshot (docs / SysML / code atomise) | Luna | `gpt-5.6-luna-medium` |
| Unclear | Grok | `cursor-grok-4.5-low` |

Luna = high-volume pin_map / atomise / snapshot loops (cost-sensitive); not peak planning (Grok), visual review (Kimi), or web search (Gemini).
Allowlist drift: same family, current non-fast slug. **Never** `*-fast` / FAST. No blind fan-out. Higher Grok only if user asks.
